Over `ssh-ng://`, `SSHStore::setOptions` sends nothing, so the remote never
learns `--keep-failed`. It deletes a failed build's directory, and the build
hook still warns that the remote kept it (`build-remote.cc:328`).
`build-remote.sh:86` then fails once its first builder speaks `ssh-ng://`.
Lillecarl/nix#413, nixidae/nixidae#1242.

--- a/src/libstore/ssh-store.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/ssh-store.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "nix/util/pool.hh"
 #include "nix/store/ssh.hh"
 #include "nix/store/store-registration.hh"
+#include "nix/store/globals.hh"

 namespace nix {

@@ -96,6 +97,26 @@
            forward-cores or forward-overridden-cores that only
            override the requested settings.
         */
+        /* `--keep-failed` must reach the remote, or it deletes the build
+           directory while `build-remote.cc` warns that it kept it
+           (Lillecarl/nix#413). `LegacySSHStore` sends `keepFailed` in its
+           build options. The fixed fields go too, as `SetOptions` has no
+           optional ones: in the build hook they are the client's, with
+           `max-jobs = 1` (`build-remote.cc`). No overrides go: in the hook
+           every setting counts as overridden, `store` and `builders`
+           included. */
+        if (!settings.keepFailed)
+            return;
+        conn.to << WorkerProto::Op::SetOptions << settings.keepFailed << settings.getWorkerSettings().keepGoing
+                << settings.getWorkerSettings().tryFallback << verbosity << settings.getWorkerSettings().maxBuildJobs
+                << settings.getWorkerSettings().maxSilentTime << true << (settings.verboseBuild ? lvlError : lvlVomit)
+                << 0 // obsolete log type
+                << 0 /* obsolete print build trace */
+                << settings.getLocalSettings().buildCores << settings.getWorkerSettings().useSubstitutes
+                << 0; // no overrides
+        auto ex = conn.processStderrReturn();
+        if (ex)
+            std::rethrow_exception(ex);
     };
 };

